## Axle repairs and services

Everything from routine axle maintenance to the work that follows a failure:

- Axle replacements
- Wheel bearing replacements
- Differential repairs
- Hub and spindle repairs
- Axle seal replacements
- Driveshaft repairs
- Alignment and balancing services

## Preventative maintenance for axles

Axles are worth inspecting on a schedule because the failure mode is expensive
and the warning is quiet. We inspect for wear, lubricate against friction and
heat, and adjust alignment so the axle is not fighting the road it is on.
Catching a bearing early is a bearing; missing it is a hub, a spindle and a tow.

An axle rarely fails on its own account. [Driveline
problems](/articles/from-u-joints-to-axle-shafts-how-driveline-problems-travel-down-to-your-axles)
travel down the chain into the differential and the shafts, which is why we look
upstream of the part that broke.

